/*****************************************************************************
    jitJPd -- THE DEGRADE CITIZEN. The rung that expects a NON-ZERO count.

    jitDegrade is docs/jit.md S0's crossover policy made concrete: an uncovered
    construct falls to the interpreted body and the fall is COUNTED. After the
    iterator rework it had ZERO call sites, so every ladder rung's
    `degrade count = 0` was VACUOUS -- a true assertion that nothing could move.

    T1's forked leaves gave it its first real citizens. A Buffer target has no
    emitter, so `+=` on one reaches a degrade arm, the interpreted body runs, and
    THE COUNTER MOVES.

    ⚠ THIS FIXTURE ASSERTS A NON-ZERO COUNT ON PURPOSE, inverting every other
    rung. That inversion is the whole point: it is what proves the other rungs'
    zeros are load-bearing rather than decorative. If this ever reports 0, the
    degrade arms stopped firing and every `degrade count = 0` in the fleet went
    back to being unfalsifiable.
    ⚠⚠ RE-PINNED 2026-09-25 (Tony's ruling: += answers on the jitted road per
    fire, no degrade, no fallback). The Buffer += no longer degrades -- an operator
    with members is fired at RUN time through jitOpFireRT, and a Buffer target is
    answered by opPlusEQ's own arm, x then xx, exactly as the interpreted road.
    So the citizen's SUBJECT moved and its JOB did not: the counter must still be
    seen to move, or every zero in the ladder is vacuous again. The body now also
    carries a cerr, which has no emitter and degrades by name. The Buffer += stays
    in the same body as a VALUE row, jitted beside interpreted.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitLadder);
define
    jpBuf buffer;
    jpBufI buffer;
    jitJPd code={ jpBuf += "x"; cerr "JPD emit-time sink":; };
    jitJPdI code={ jpBufI += "x"; };
    ;

print "JPD jitting a body whose cerr has no emitter (must DEGRADE) beside a Buffer += (must NOT):":;
testing(jitJPd);
cerr "JPD jit 1 [" jpBuf "]":;
jitRefire();
cerr "JPD jit 2 [" jpBuf "]":;
jitJPdI();
cerr "JPD int 1 [" jpBufI "]":;
jitJPdI();
cerr "JPD int 2 [" jpBufI "]":;
print "JPD SENTINEL":;
stop();
